adr: 0363
file: runtime/pasrt_posix.c
kills: lib_process_execute
why: The deadline is recorded and never armed, so case 19's child -- a shell whose grandchild holds the pipe for thirty seconds -- holds this side for thirty seconds and then answers `after`, ok = true. The case's `under 10s` and its `ok` both turn, and the harness's per-case timeout is what would have said so had the case not.
--- old
  pr->has_deadline = a->deadline_ms > 0;
--- new
  pr->has_deadline = 0;
